INSERT INTO "messages" VALUES('f37fe301','96eb91fc','f37fe301','thinking','{"content":"**Updating Deletion Mechanics**\n\nI''ve successfully finished implementing the delete button modifications within `config_app.py` for both Claude and Gemini. I also updated `claude_oauth_manager.py` to allow deletion of the active profile and properly clean up its associated tokens. Gemini was already properly cleaning up tokens, so no change was necessary.\n\n\n**Analyzing Anti-Fraud Triggers**\n\nI''m now focusing on the anti-fraud mechanisms of Claude. The user''s question highlights a potential issue with token transfer triggering a block. I believe that copying and moving Claude cookies, especially the `sessionKey` or `access_token`, across different network contexts (IPs, User-Agents, etc.) is likely the root cause, triggering Anthropic''s fraud detection. This confirms the user''s concerns about the authorization method''s potential dangers.\n\n\n**Investigating Fraud Triggers**\n\nI''m digging deeper into Anthropic''s fraud detection triggers. It seems rapid IP/location changes, especially to datacenter IPs, are a major red flag. User-Agent and fingerprint mismatches, like using a token minted in Chrome with a basic `curl` script, also set off alarms. Sudden, intense request bursts after a token transfer are a third significant trigger. My recommendation will emphasize the inherent risks of token transfer, especially considering Claude''s tracking of `sessionKey` associations.\n\n\n","status":"done","duration_ms":3478}','left','finish',0,1790228178772,NULL);
